WEBVTT

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.940
Oh my, that smells delicious.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.160
Mommy!

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:12.360
It's yummy!

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.180
<i>Daddy...</i>

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:21.380
<i>Mommy...</i>

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:26.590
Kotarou.

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:29.000
Why don't we eat together again?

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:31.860
Yeah.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:13.320
President! Good news!

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:14.420
What is it?

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:18.780
Episode 4: "Until We Return to Those Days"

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:18.040
I met someone who seems knowledgeable 
about unidentified mysterious animals!

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:19.000
And?

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.920
Come on. Please give me
a slightly happier reaction!

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.450
He seems like the real deal!

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:26.800
Even if that were true,
why would it make me happy?

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.360
<i>Haroken! Haroken!</i>

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.440
Wouldn't it only benefit you,
 and no one else?

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.310
No! Th-That's not it at all!

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:36.340
I-I'm doing all this for the 
occult research club's benefit!

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:38.720
<i>You lose!</i>

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:39.620
Darn.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.430
Got it.

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:50.000
So, where is this elderly gentleman?

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.980
There's supposed to be a ramen stand
somewhere around here.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:54.880
Don't see one.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:57.110
Aren't stands only around at night?

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:58.640
You could be right.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.680
If only Shizuru were here.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.680
She's apparently a regular.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:05.990
Damn. I can't get through to her at all.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.770
Do you know anything, Class Rep?

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:10.120
Shizuru may not look it, 
but she's a busy girl.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:14.160
Come to think of it, she did say
she had other things to do.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.390
On that note,

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:17.560
if Shizuru isn't here, I'll take my leave.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.880
Wait, um, we have club activities, you know?

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.060
I've had enough of this.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:25.490
Come to me once you've found that
elderly gentleman or whatever.

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:26.640
Okay...

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.890
No way that happened.

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:42.930
I'm pretty sure he said something 
about an antiques shop.

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:47.830
Watch where you're walking.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:49.910
Don't you have eyes?

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:51.580
I-I'm sorry.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:52.750
You...

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.140
What's your name?

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.500
It's Tennouji.

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.860
Tennouji-kun, huh?

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:03.260
Wow, so you are living
 as an everyday student.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:05.250
Um, what is it?

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:08.980
Oh, there's a bunch of 
show-off brats around here,

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:10.510
so you should be careful.

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:12.180
Right... Thank you.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:27.110
Oh, I should've asked that guy
if he knew about the shop.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:35.290
Wow. He just warned me about this, too.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.800
What school you from, punk?

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:39.290
I'm from Kaza High...

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:40.420
Kazamatsuri?

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:43.370
That uniform! Yoshino-san's place, eh?

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:44.230
Yoshino?

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:46.470
Do you mean Yoshino Haruhiko?

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:49.100
That's Yoshino-<i>san</i> to you, ya loser!

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.210
He's the king!

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:51.060
King?

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:53.680
That guy's the slum king!

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:57.880
These rotten, mangy slums used to
be ruled by drugs and violence,

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:01.640
but he transformed them into
a den of wolves with his fists alone.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.000
Seriously?

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.450
That Yoshino?

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.970
How d'ya know the king?

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:08.490
We're just buddies...

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:09.820
Buddies?

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:11.200
With the king?

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:13.750
Countin' on ya.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:17.880
Sorry to make you go out of 
your way for a kid like me.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.400
Don't sweat it. I'm a first-year,

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.420
so if you're the same age as the king,
I'm a year younger.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:24.260
What?!

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:25.710
<i>This guy's younger than me?!</i>

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:27.450
<i>That's the biggest shock today!</i>

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:28.700
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.800
<i>I feel like I wasted my time
 buttering him up.</i>

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:33.810
What's up, bro?
Helluva scary face you got there.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.360
How long 'til you find it?

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:38.270
I can't wait around forever.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:40.310
Your attitude changed awfully quick.

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:45.660
That shop over there is
probably the one you're after.

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.070
You're life savers.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.340
No problem.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:50.880
If you're the king's buddy, 
then you're also a wolf.

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:54.080
We of the Wolf Pack will gladly
help you out anytime.

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:00.960
Welcome.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.960
Oh, it's you.

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:04.260
Hello.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.850
I'm surprised you found this place.

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:09.060
I forgot to give you my business card before.

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:11.740
I made good use of my connections
and sleuthing skills.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:14.940
Shizuru!

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:16.730
Kotarou!

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.920
This is where you were?

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:22.340
I called your cell but couldn't 
get through to you at all.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:23.480
Sorry.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:26.740
I'd kept it turned off to 
save on electricity costs.

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:29.610
What's the point of
having a cell phone, then?

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:32.270
By the way,

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:35.740
you two seem to be rather close
for students in different years.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:37.340
When did you two get to know each other?

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:39.230
Oh, well...

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:40.370
That was...

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:45.380
Going to a committee meeting?

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:48.630
I was just about to head out myself.
Want to go together?

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:52.140
What's your name?

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.390
Shizuru.

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:55.140
I'm Tennouji the Hero.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:57.590
Hero-senpai?

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:58.900
Kotarou.

00:06:58.900 --> 00:06:59.890
Kotarou.

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:01.750
Where's your meeting?

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.050
The Disciplay Committee!

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:05.770
It was a perfectly ordinary encounter.

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:07.030
What is it?!

00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:12.260
Hey, stop, stop! Stop it!

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:11.480
By the way, Tennouji-kun, was it?

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:12.610
Why did you come here?

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:15.290
For what we talked about before!

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:19.620
Tell me about the unidentified animals
your friend saw a long time ago!

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:21.830
Oh, that's right.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:22.880
Very well.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.670
They're out of focus, so it's hard to tell.

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:33.180
They could just be wild animals, but here
they look like mysterious creatures.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:38.420
<i>They're different from the ones I saw.</i>

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:40.930
And, about this next photo...

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.560
I'm glad you found these useful.

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:46.660
This is awesome, really.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:48.130
Good for you, Kotarou.

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:50.940
Now you're one step closer 
to the president's bosom.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:52.850
What does she mean, "bosom"?

00:07:52.850 --> 00:07:54.780
Sh-She means in a romantic sense!

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.340
Oh, right. Tennouji-kun.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:57.450
Please take my card.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.450
<b>Pratfall!</b>

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.450
<b>Esaka Sougen</b>

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.450
<b>I Don't Intend to See Your
 Filthy Mug Ever Again</b>

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:01.520
Is something the matter?

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:02.490
Oh, no!

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:04.060
It's a lovely card!

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:06.470
It's five million for one.

00:08:06.470 --> 00:08:08.020
Could you please pay up?

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:08.590
Huh?

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:09.580
Er...

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:11.220
Why?!

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:14.580
Who would pay such a fortune for

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:16.710
scrap paper?!

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:19.720
Um, the coffee was delicious.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:22.330
Come by anytime you like.

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:24.620
I'd be delighted to have a young customer.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:30.940
Kotarou, motivating yourself is good,

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:33.840
but your obsession with breasts
will disturb public order.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:37.490
You make it sound like I'm only 
working hard for the breasts.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:38.900
You're not?

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:43.320
Hold on.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:48.410
I got a huge haul again today.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:49.330
What's that for?

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:50.840
Gonna feed it to pigeons or something?

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:52.860
I'm going to eat it.

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:54.130
Is that any good?

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.890
It's not bad if you know how to use it.

00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:01.890
What is it this time?

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.640
CDs in cart

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.640
Listen to those nostalgic
tunes one more time!

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.640
<b>All 100 yen!!</b>

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:04.280
It's a second-hand shop.

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:07.270
Please look!

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:10.270
A plethora of photos which close in
on the mysteries of Kazamatsuri!

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:14.030
I hear photos like these
were all the rage a while ago.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:15.680
Let's investigate them!

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:18.240
No. I feel like my kill count
is going to go up today.

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:20.010
What about club activities...

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:21.030
Kotarou!

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.290
The CD I bought for you yesterday?

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:26.230
What CD is that?

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:27.790
Touka's favorite songs.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.290
Who's Touka?

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:32.060
Shizuru-chan!

00:09:32.060 --> 00:09:33.550
Nishikujou-sensei?

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:35.640
I can't listen to it.

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:37.520
What? Is the disc scratched up?

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:38.800
I don't have a player.

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:40.030
Oh...

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:41.870
Why not just go buy one, then?

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:42.990
Hey, rich girl.

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:44.490
You buy one for her, then.

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:46.310
Why do I have to buy her one?

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:50.190
It is true that Chihaya-san's 
family is well off,

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:53.940
but she has a limited monthly
 allowance, Dimwitarou-kun.

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:57.200
You're hanging around the clubroom 
like it's natural now, huh?

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:59.640
Can't you work it out somehow, Tennouji?

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:02.850
I wonder if there are any 
spare players around?

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:05.700
Oh, I do have one at my house.

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:08.390
Hup...

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:09.990
Here it is!

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:15.670
It's still got the songs
I put on it ages ago,

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:17.220
so let me know if you want to add more.

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:19.220
You don't listen to music anymore?

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:20.350
I do,

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:21.350
with this.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:22.440
What about this?

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:23.810
You won't use it anymore?

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:25.940
You ask some difficult questions.

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:27.380
You don't want to talk about it?

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:29.350
That's fine, then. I'm sorry.

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:30.710
Oh, nah...

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:33.360
Whenever I didn't want to listen
to my parents scold me,

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:35.180
I used to block them out with this.

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:37.240
I was such an idiot back then.

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:38.820
You were a rebellious kid?

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:40.860
Yeah. It was a dark chapter in my life.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.530
I learned one of your secrets.

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:45.230
I wouldn't go that far.

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:46.620
It is embarrassing, though.

00:10:47.050 --> 00:10:49.560
I'll treasure this.

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:50.650
Go ahead and do that.

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:52.330
It did no wrong.

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:56.120
By reading it out loud repeatedly,

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:57.920
you'll naturally pick up on the meaning.

00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:58.600
<i>Thanks to the president's shikigamis,</i>

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:59.120
Moving on...

00:10:58.600 --> 00:11:01.430
<i>the ribbon ghost stopped 
showing up in my room...</i>

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:05.220
<i>But what was she doing there?</i>

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:06.470
<i>Also...</i>

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.690
<i>That guy's definitely bad news.</i>

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:14.310
<i>And here I thought things had 
finally gotten peaceful lately.</i>

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:21.410
Huh? Why did the door open by itself?

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:29.580
<i>Th-They can't see her?!</i>

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.890
What're you making creepy noises for?

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:49.890
I wonder what that was about.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:50.890
Okay, let's get back to the lesson.

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.340
Now she's showing up in broad daylight!

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:05.030
I'll have to ask the president to
deploy shikigamis in school, too!

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:07.400
Kotarou.

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:10.290
Shizuru?

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:15.360
What's wrong? You're drenched in sweat.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.180
Nothing.

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:19.230
Anyway, have you gotten 
the hang of using it yet?

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:19.980
Perfectly.

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:21.670
I've been listening to it since yesterday.

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:22.800
Really? That's great.

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:25.550
I'd like you to join me 
for a little while today.

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.360
A sudden confession of love?

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:32.380
You told me one of your secrets,

00:12:32.380 --> 00:12:35.060
so I want to tell you one of mine.

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:37.070
One of your secrets?

00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:37.900
Yes.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:41.570
Um, what's your relationship with each other?

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:42.820
It's a secret.

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:46.320
Could you at least tell me
where we're headed?

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:50.700
The home Shizuru-chan was born and raised in.

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:52.450
Oh, really?

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:54.500
Say, Tennouji-kun.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:56.640
I'm a bit of a liar,

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:59.560
but Shizuru-chan can probably 
only tell the truth.

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:02.960
So I would like you to trust
what she tells you.

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:08.700
On that note, go by yourselves
the rest of the way.

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:15.600
Kotarou, over here.

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:17.700
Coming.

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:24.090
Looks like nobody's home.

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:30.450
Shall we wait?

00:13:34.340 --> 00:13:38.840
<i>We're your friendly 
neighborhood recyclers...</i>

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:47.810
Shizuru, I think they're home, actually.

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:49.090
Yeah.

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:50.320
In that case—

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:51.180
Oh?

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:57.740
Have I met you somewhere before?

00:13:57.740 --> 00:13:58.230
Huh?

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:01.280
I see.

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:03.020
That's an unfamiliar uniform.

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:04.440
Did you come from somewhere far away?

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:05.240
No, um...

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:08.990
But...

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:09.610
Please.

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:13.370
Those roses are super pretty.

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:15.240
Oh, thank you!

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:18.420
Those roses have been around for years now.

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:20.900
I don't remember when I planted them, though.

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:21.790
I see.

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:23.260
What's up?

00:14:23.260 --> 00:14:26.670
This girl said the roses in 
our garden are very pretty.

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:29.180
Would you like to take one with you?

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:29.950
It's okay.

00:14:29.950 --> 00:14:31.430
I've seen them plenty already.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:32.700
Let's go.

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:34.940
Sure...

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:36.680
Come again!

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:39.800
Welcome home!

00:14:41.260 --> 00:14:42.990
We're home, Shizu-chan.

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:44.690
Were you a good girl, Shizuka?

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:46.280
Yeah, I was taking a nap!

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:47.990
Shizuka?

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:49.200
My little sister.

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:52.440
What's going on?

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:53.990
This doesn't make any sense.

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:57.560
Mom and Dad don't know about me.

00:14:57.560 --> 00:14:58.220
Huh?

00:14:58.220 --> 00:14:59.540
But aren't they your parents?

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:03.290
Kotarou, my name.

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:05.550
Nakatsu Shizuru.

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:07.660
My name?

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:08.680
Like I said...

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:10.120
Huh? Uh...

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:11.160
You can't remember?

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:12.470
No, that shouldn't be...

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:14.600
I can do that.

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:17.390
My name is...

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:18.080
Wait!

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.280
I'll remember it right now.

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:20.980
Um, um...

00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:24.110
Shi... Shizu...

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:25.340
Shizuru!

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:26.680
That's it, Shizuru!

00:15:26.970 --> 00:15:30.030
There's no way I'd ever forget your name!

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:32.040
Kotarou!

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:38.120
So, your parents forgot about you 
due to that power from before?

00:15:38.300 --> 00:15:41.080
At first, I couldn't control it
as well as I can now.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.250
So I ended up overdoing it.

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:49.670
I'm told that my power can cause severe
memory defects and severed synapses.

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:54.320
We were an ordinary family, if a little poor.

00:15:54.710 --> 00:15:56.660
Dad was kind.

00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:58.010
So was Mom.

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:00.520
We all got along great.

00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:04.060
Dad would often grill saury for us.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:05.740
It was my favorite.

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:08.360
The guts were bitter,
and I didn't like them much.

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:10.530
Dad would eat them for me.

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:16.610
Dad told me to I'd be able to
eat them once I grew up.

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:18.990
Mom told me that becoming an adult

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:24.540
meant becoming able to eat bitter things.

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:27.520
To mark my entering elementary school,

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:29.900
I planted flowers with Mom.

00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:31.550
They were roses.

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:33.590
Dad handled the heavy lifting.

00:16:33.910 --> 00:16:37.180
We all hoped they bloomed into pretty roses.

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:40.810
One day, we all went to a festival together.

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:43.230
It was the Kazamatsuri Harvest Festa.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:47.520
On the way home, Dad showed us a new house.

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:51.830
He said, "This is our new home."

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:55.050
I asked, "Can we afford it?"

00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:58.600
Dad said, "I'll work hard for all of us."

00:16:58.970 --> 00:17:01.950
Mom was so happy she cried a little.

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:05.540
It happened soon after that.

00:17:13.990 --> 00:17:18.000
My friends used to tell me my
good luck charms were very effective.

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:20.310
"Pain, pain, go away!"

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:25.710
"Go away, go away, go away!"

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:27.700
Daddy!

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:29.360
Mommy!

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:34.190
Go away.

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:35.360
Go away.

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:36.490
Go away!

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:37.560
Go away!

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:45.500
Hey, there's people here!

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:46.740
Civilians...

00:17:46.740 --> 00:17:47.900
Call the EMTs.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:48.710
But...

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:52.200
If we desert ordinary civilians,
who are we supposed to protect?

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:52.750
Sir!

00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:55.530
Those bastards...

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:57.960
Only the sniper team needs to pursue!

00:17:57.960 --> 00:18:00.900
Everyone else, look for survivors 
and extinguish the fires in this area!

00:18:00.900 --> 00:18:02.760
All three of them are breathing!

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:05.020
Be careful with the man's back.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:07.570
That glass shard may have reached his lungs.

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:08.520
Okay!

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:10.020
Let's save some lives!

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:11.260
Humans are top priority!

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:12.620
Save the stray cats, too!

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:14.940
Don't let anyone die in vain!

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:16.490
Yes, sir!

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:21.410
Her eye healed? What's going on?

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:22.780
There's no other way to look at it.

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:24.910
Call the chief. This is an emergency!

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:46.660
Did you place a good luck charm on me?

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:47.480
Yeah!

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:48.520
I see.

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:49.690
Thank you, Shizuru.

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:51.110
I'm sorry.

00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:53.420
Our new home is gone.

00:18:53.420 --> 00:18:54.940
I don't mind.

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:01.090
So weird!

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:02.520
I wonder what's with that color.

00:19:01.090 --> 00:19:03.070
Let's keep away from her.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:03.070
Maybe she's sick...

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:10.080
Mom cowered in fear at the sight of fire.

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:13.320
I wanted to cook saury, but I held out.

00:19:14.140 --> 00:19:16.030
Then, a man I didn't know told them this:

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:19.340
If I went to a certain 
institution and stayed there,

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:22.970
he would give Mom and Dad lots of money.

00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:26.390
I answered that I would go.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.790
I came home that weekend.

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:35.020
I'm home!

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:39.280
Mom and Dad were fighting again.

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:43.410
The sudden influx of money had changed them.

00:19:43.780 --> 00:19:45.990
I panicked and tried to stop them,

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:47.720
but they didn't listen to me.

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:50.660
<i>They used to be so kind...</i>

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:55.620
<i>We all got along so well...</i>

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:03.800
<i>Is it my fault?</i>

00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:06.700
What happened?

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:10.060
They lost several years' worth of memories.

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:13.080
When I wished for them to 
return to their old selves,

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:15.560
they forgot almost everything 
about me as well.

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:18.320
I let my power go out of control.

00:20:19.100 --> 00:20:20.280
They can't be cured?

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:23.850
I mean, I remembered your name 
right away earlier, didn't I?

00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:26.200
The extent of damage is on
a whole other level.

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:28.950
Kotarou.

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:37.570
Thank you for coming with me today.

00:20:38.080 --> 00:20:40.340
I was happy earlier.

00:20:51.070 --> 00:20:55.140
Are you affiliated with the institution
Shizuru went to, Sensei?

00:20:55.140 --> 00:20:56.980
Something like that, yes.

00:20:57.420 --> 00:21:00.150
Was Shizuru born with that power?

00:21:01.680 --> 00:21:03.590
Our organization thinks of it

00:21:03.590 --> 00:21:06.410
as "the power to produce medicine."

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:07.710
Organization?

00:21:07.710 --> 00:21:09.410
The power to create medicine?

00:21:09.880 --> 00:21:11.820
Um, who are you all, exactly—

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:12.760
Hold on, Tennouji-kun.

00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:15.800
You mustn't pry into a 
woman's secrets too deeply!

00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:18.840
You can't say that after
I've already gotten this involved.

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:20.880
<i>I see.</i>

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:22.170
<i>She did it then, too.</i>

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:25.150
Do you know how much 
Shizuru-chan has in the bank?

00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:25.680
No.

00:21:25.850 --> 00:21:26.640
Listen up...

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:27.600
Whisper, whisper...

00:21:27.600 --> 00:21:28.860
S-Seriously?

00:21:28.860 --> 00:21:31.100
Th-Then why is she living 
like she has no money?

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:32.750
She's saving it.

00:21:32.750 --> 00:21:34.360
She says she's going to buy a house.

00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:36.850
She might also be punishing herself.

00:21:37.050 --> 00:21:38.040
No way.

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:39.740
It's not like she did anything wrong.

00:21:39.740 --> 00:21:41.180
What do you think, Tennouji-kun?

00:21:41.180 --> 00:21:43.920
Was that too much for you?
Would you have rather not known?

00:21:45.510 --> 00:21:47.120
Of course not.

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:51.850
If anything, I'm worried that
I'll end up wanting to know even more.

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:58.120
Hey, wake up!

00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:01.170
I had a dream.

00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:02.130
Wh-What kind?

00:22:02.390 --> 00:22:04.280
I'm even more Shizuru about worried.

00:22:04.280 --> 00:22:06.130
If anything, I'll end up knowing to want.

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:08.670
<i>It's mostly what I actually said,</i>

00:22:08.670 --> 00:22:10.740
<i>but it's so out of order, it makes no sense.</i>

00:22:11.620 --> 00:22:13.850
Okay, please make sure she gets home.

00:22:13.850 --> 00:22:14.930
Sure thing!

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:15.740
See you.

00:22:17.810 --> 00:22:19.440
Superpowers, huh?

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:21.130
Come to think of it,

00:22:21.130 --> 00:22:23.160
I've got a massive secret of my own.

00:22:24.280 --> 00:22:27.150
I guess we can get along 
as a superpowered duo.

00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:36.750
No way! It's filthy!
I don't want to touch it!

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:37.740
What the heck?!

00:22:37.740 --> 00:22:39.500
All you have to do is pick up the ball!

00:22:39.780 --> 00:22:41.630
I'm telling you, I don't want to!

00:22:41.630 --> 00:22:44.000
Hey! No fighting!

00:22:44.330 --> 00:22:46.140
One ball, coming right up!

00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:48.260
Would you like fries with that?

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:52.220
Being a clean freak is all well and good,

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:54.140
but take it too far,
and it could cause trouble.

00:22:54.320 --> 00:22:56.370
I don't want to hear your complaints!

00:22:56.370 --> 00:22:59.140
Why am I getting criticized here?

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:01.780
Couldn't you at least pick up a ball?

00:23:01.780 --> 00:23:03.530
Chihaya, knock it off.

00:23:03.530 --> 00:23:04.750
He's right, Chi-chan.

00:23:04.750 --> 00:23:06.780
Nobody's in the wrong.

00:23:06.960 --> 00:23:09.150
That's not it. I don't want to touch them.

00:23:09.300 --> 00:23:11.180
Huh? What did you say?

00:23:11.180 --> 00:23:12.220
I said stop it.

00:23:12.220 --> 00:23:13.780
I don't want to touch the flowers!

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:14.410
Huh?

00:23:14.410 --> 00:23:16.870
You're saying even flowers are dirty?

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:18.500
Wh-Why?

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:20.500
The flowers are so pretty, too...

00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:23.720
I don't want to touch what 
I don't want to touch!

00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:25.580
Ow!

00:23:25.580 --> 00:23:27.490
Wh-What was that for?!

00:23:27.490 --> 00:23:28.170
Chi-chan!

00:23:28.330 --> 00:23:29.560
Hey, Class Rep!

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:33.980
I-I think you have a messed-up mind
for feeling that way!

00:23:43.870 --> 00:23:45.590
Listen, class rep.

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:47.780
You could be a little more tactful...

00:23:49.530 --> 00:23:53.780
D-Do you think I'm living 
this way because I want to?!
